                        "recommendationid": "239754146",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198063465895",
                            "num_reviews": 703,
                            "playtime_forever": 217,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 217,
                            "playtime_at_review": 217,
                            "last_played": 1794186225
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I really like the concept, execution and design of Nonogram - a simple pixel painting game, where you try to make the images that the title hints towards. It takes a bit of risk on some of the later puzzles, as there's just not enough data to work with when it comes to a starting point - a problem the smaller puzzles don't have (usually anyways). There are, however, some puzzles that have some questionable slip-ups in the filled in grid, and i found a few of the images themselves were a bit questionable in design. Still, for the amount, quantity and general quality, I'm a fan of how it all turns out. Nice, relaxing, thoughtful, Nonogram is an enjoyable experience, and something I found interesting.",
